# NUMERICS: division and modulo signs. `/` on two integers truncates toward
# zero; `%` is FLOORED, taking the DIVISOR's sign — Lua's law, and Idol's since
# 2026-08-15 (`docs/rulings.md` § "Modulo and floor division").
#
# This header used to cite `§12 B-4` for a truncating `%` and to note that it
# "diverges from Lua, which floors". **§12 B-4 does not exist in either tree**,
# and the divergence had no warrant in any document that does.
# expect: -3 -3 1 -1
# @corpus current
a = -7 / 2
b = 7 / -2
c = -7 % 2
d = 7 % -2
print("{a} {b} {c} {d}")
0
